  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed shop front includes the installation of an On-Demand Grocery hatch within the front elevation yet would fail to provide adequate off-street servicing arrangements for commercial vehicles and general servicing. The use of the proposed delivery hatch would detrimentally impact upon the safe operation of the road network, as its access across the pavement on St Johns Road would hinder the convenient and safe passage of pedestrians.\r\nThe proposal would therefore fail to comply with policies LP2, LP50 and LP51 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023), policies T1, T2, T4 and T7 of the London Plan (2021) and policies TR4 and DP3 of the NPPF (2026).\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
